# Loop read-only (opt-in per project)

## Adoption gate

Loop CI monitoring applies **only when** the repository root contains **`.cursor/LOOP.md`** (committed project rules).

If `.cursor/LOOP.md` is **absent**:

- Do **not** arm `/loop` or `ci-watch-loop` proactively
- Do **not** fail the verification gate or block task completion
- Emit `Loop watch: SKIPPED (reason: no-loop-md)` if loops are relevant to the conversation

## Policy (hard)

- **Read-only in loops** — no `git push`, `git commit`, `gh workflow run`, `gh run rerun`, or file edits inside `/loop` prompts
- **No fix-until-green loops** — do not loop until CI passes; fix in foreground or user invokes `/babysit` explicitly
- **No auto-start** — never arm a loop without user opt-in
- **Not a done gate** — loops do not replace project verification in `DEVELOPMENT.md`
- **Local session only** — `/loop` does not run in cloud agents

## Suggest-not-block (when adopted)

When `.cursor/LOOP.md` exists, a PR to **`<BASE_BRANCH>`** is open, CI checks are pending, and the user is waiting:

- **Suggest once**: consider `ci-watch-loop` skill or a read-only `/loop 5m …` prompt — opt-in
- If the developer declines or ignores, **continue** — do not block
- Do **not** suggest `/babysit` in the same suggestion as `/loop`

Local skill gates non-`<BASE_BRANCH>` bases with `SKIPPED (reason: not-<base>-pr)`.

## Babysit boundary

- **`/loop`** — read-only monitoring (this rule)
- **`/babysit`** — active merge prep with pushes; **user-invoked only** — do not suggest proactively when suggesting loops

